<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-1366] Remove legacy alias feature for JDBC</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-1366</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-999&quot; title=&quot;Support alias for JDBC properties&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-999&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-999&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; enables users to use JDBC with it&apos;s own prefix. But &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-1012&quot; title=&quot;Support alias for interpreter&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-1012&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-1012&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; finished, it makes Zeppelin support general way to use aliases for all interpreters. Thus JDBC sugar is not useful anymore and it also contains a small bug. It should be removed.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
