&lt;p&gt;    I think it changes way of configuration. From single jdbc interpreter setting manages multiple jdbc connection, to individual interpreter setting manage single jdbc connection.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    How about remove non-default jdbc connection configurations from default properties and documentation?&lt;br/&gt;
    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/blob/master/jdbc/src/main/resources/interpreter-setting.json&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/blob/master/jdbc/src/main/resources/interpreter-setting.json&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
